Vertex programs compiled ahead: as the title makes a vertex shader (CreateVertexShader, mostly while a level loads)
its program is compiled on threads of their own into the shader cache, for the declaration's inputs as a draw most
likely reads them (raw, and converted on the CPU), so the draw finds it there instead of compiling it then. The hitch
log counts the shaders draws still compile, by kind, and those compiled ahead.

